---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { launch, launchLabel, site, sourceUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Roadmap" description="The v0.20 launch baseline, current integration work and future proposals, with source links and no invented shipping dates.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Direction / Built in the open</span><h1>What’s taking shape.</h1><p class="lead">A clear view of the product, the work being finished and the ideas that still need testing.</p></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>The v0.20 product.</h2><p>The {launchLabel} brings the existing frontend together with queue workflows, background tasks and expanded context. <a href="/releases/#launch-baseline">Source and publication status →</a></p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Integrated</span><div><h3>Commands, output and continuity</h3><p>A persistent composer and shell, live sessions, serial queue, execution timeline, output selection, Copy Actions, reviewed reports and comparisons.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/execution/">Execution workflows <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Integrated</span><div><h3>Work alongside the shell</h3><p>Session-owned background tasks, managed Claude Code beta, worktree tools, read-only GitHub inspection and a larger native module catalog. The experimental workspace sidebar remains Off by default.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/integrations/">Tools and workspaces <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Finishing the launch.</h2><p>Final integration and release validation are separate from the product descriptions. A specification alone does not prove a finished terminal interaction.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Validation</span><div><h3>First-run onboarding</h3><p>Reactive Horizon, selection-reactive Aurora, transparent Vespyr compositing and the transition into the composer are wired into the documented candidate. The remaining work is final release integration, follow-up behavior review and physical acceptance, not inventing the interface from a proposal.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/setup/">Setup and first run <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Validation</span><div><h3>Real hosts and release evidence</h3><p>Physical Ghostty and Terminal.app testing, Linux and WSL 2 limits, the final immutable tag and Homebrew availability must be checked before launch.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/reference/physical-qa/">Candidate QA checklist <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Future proposals.</h2><p>Directions worth investigating, not scheduled commitments. Scope, feasibility, security and design approval can change what eventually ships.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Planned · Future</span><div><h3>Learn the command line by doing</h3><p>Guided Bash/zsh lessons, practice files, helpful feedback and resumable progress. Strong real-shell isolation must be verified, or execution must be explicitly simulated or disabled.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/learn/">Explore future Learn Mode <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Research / proposal</span><div><h3>Broader integrations, without blurred authority</h3><p>Additional managed-agent adapters, workflow tool integrations and stronger isolation for executable mods require independent capability and security evidence.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/339`}>Agent adapters · #339 <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/341`}>Executable-mod isolation · #341 <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><p class="muted measure">Reviewed {launch.verifiedAt}. See the <a href={sourceUrl('ROADMAP.md')}>source roadmap</a>, <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>public issues</a> and <a href="https://github.com/users/raiseCatError/projects/1">development Project</a> for the full context. An issue on the board is not automatically a product commitment.</p></section>
  </div>
</Base>
